This is not a sound file. It is its name.

The polite one. Four notes, descending, played when something had gone
wrong but not badly enough to deserve CHORD.WAV - a dialog you could answer,
a field you had filled in wrongly, a disk that was not in the drive yet.

CHORD.WAV was the other one, and everybody could tell them apart from the
next room.

Nothing here will play either. This desktop says what it means in the status
line at the bottom of the screen, which is slower to notice and much easier
to act on.
